  <Folder>
    <name>B1 wild trout waters</name>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Winooski River (above Lower Cabot)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Species:</b> BKT &mdash; <b>B1</b><br/><b>Watershed:</b> Winooski mainstem &amp; direct tributaries<br/>Wild brookies abundant in the mainstem above Cabot village; habitat deteriorates below the village where riparian cover is thin.<br/><b>Nearest access:</b><ul><li>Coits Pond (state fishing access) &mdash; 552 m as the crow flies, 79.9 min drive</li><li>West Hill Pond (state fishing access) &mdash; 2175 m as the crow flies, 73.9 min drive</li></ul><br/><b>Drive from inn:</b> 68.9 min<br/><b>Source:</b> <a href="https://dec.vermont.gov/sites/dec/files/wsm/mapp/docs/mp_UpperWinooskiWatershedFisheriesSummary_2017-12-15.pdf#page=6">VFWD 2017, Table 6 p.6</a><br/><b>Confidence:</b> high (VFWD 2017 Table 6)]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#pt-2e7d32</styleUrl>
