    <Placemark>
      <name>Molly's Brook (above Marshfield Dam)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Species:</b> BKT, BNT &mdash; <b>B1</b><br/><b>Watershed:</b> Winooski mainstem &amp; direct tributaries<br/>B1 above Molly's Falls Reservoir; wild brook and brown trout, occasional rainbows.<br/><b>Nearest access:</b><ul><li>Joe's Pond (state fishing access) &mdash; 1401 m as the crow flies, 70.7 min drive</li><li>Marshfield Dam (state fishing access) &mdash; 2569 m as the crow flies, 64.2 min drive</li></ul><br/><b>Drive from inn:</b> 65.8 min<br/><b>Source:</b> <a href="https://dec.vermont.gov/sites/dec/files/wsm/mapp/docs/mp_UpperWinooskiWatershedFisheriesSummary_2017-12-15.pdf#page=6">VFWD 2017, Table 6 p.6</a><br/><b>Confidence:</b> high (VFWD 2017 Table 6)]]></description>
