    <Placemark>
      <name>Dog River mainstem</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Species:</b> BKT, BNT, RBT &mdash; <b>B1</b><br/><b>Watershed:</b> Dog River<br/>Whole mainstem is B1 and managed as wild trout water; brookies only above Route 12A in Roxbury, mixed below, browns/rainbows dominate below Northfield Falls. Reduced-harvest regs on a 4.3-mile stretch in Berlin (verify current regs). Point is near the mouth.<br/><b>Nearest access:</b><ul><li>Dog River Jacuzzi Natural Area - Berlin VFD lot (2095 VT-12) &mdash; 69 m as the crow flies, 39.2 min drive</li><li>Roxbury Gap Rd / Warren Mountain Rd (the gap) &mdash; 1057 m as the crow flies, 13.1 min drive</li><li>Berlin Pond (state fishing access) &mdash; 2694 m as the crow flies, 39.8 min drive</li></ul><br/><b>Drive from inn:</b> 38.2 min<br/><b>Source:</b> <a href="https://dec.vermont.gov/sites/dec/files/wsm/mapp/docs/mp_UpperWinooskiWatershedFisheriesSummary_2017-12-15.pdf#page=7">VFWD 2017, Table 10 p.7</a><br/><b>Confidence:</b> high (VFWD 2017 Table 10)]]></description>
