    <Placemark>
      <name>Clay Brook</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Species:</b> BKT &mdash; <b>B1</b><br/><b>Watershed:</b> Mad River<br/>Wild brook trout. Crashed after a 1998 flood, recovered by 2000, then over 1,000 trout/mile every year 2001-2016 (had once been listed as impaired). Point is up near the Sugarbush base; brook follows Sugarbush Access Rd.<br/><b>Nearest access:</b><ul><li>Sugarbush - Lincoln Peak base lots (Gate House Ln) &mdash; 96 m as the crow flies, 21.7 min drive</li><li>Riverside Park (Warren, Rte 100) &mdash; 125 m as the crow flies, 10.6 min drive</li><li>Kingsbury Greenway - Wabanaki Conservation Area parking (500 Rte 100) &mdash; 415 m as the crow flies, 10.4 min drive</li></ul><br/><b>Drive from inn:</b> 20.9 min<br/><b>Source:</b> <a href="https://dec.vermont.gov/sites/dec/files/wsm/mapp/docs/mp_UpperWinooskiWatershedFisheriesSummary_2017-12-15.pdf#page=7">VFWD 2017, Table 11 p.7</a><br/><b>Confidence:</b> high (VFWD 2017 Table 11)]]></description>
