    <Placemark>
      <name>Lincoln Brook</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Species:</b> BKT<br/><b>Watershed:</b> Mad River<br/>Wild brook trout. Follows Lincoln Gap Rd (unpaved near the top, closed in winter). 2019 culvert replacement on Lincoln Gap Rd reconnected headwater habitat (Valley Reporter 2019-06-28, https://www.valleyreporter.com/index.php/news/local-news/13423-mad-river-watching-and-fishing).<br/><b>Nearest access:</b><ul><li>Lincoln Gap - Long Trail trailhead &mdash; 760 m as the crow flies, 23.2 min drive</li><li>Warren Falls lot (3919 Rte 100) &mdash; 847 m as the crow flies, 15.9 min drive</li><li>Warren village - covered bridge / Main St &mdash; 919 m as the crow flies, 13.8 min drive</li></ul><br/><b>Drive from inn:</b> 21.5 min<br/><b>Source:</b> <a href="https://dec.vermont.gov/sites/dec/files/wsm/mapp/docs/mp_UpperWinooskiWatershedFisheriesSummary_2017-12-15.pdf#page=15">VFWD 2017, narrative p.15</a><br/><b>Confidence:</b> medium (Google Places 2026-09-23)]]></description>
