    <Placemark>
      <name>Mills Brook</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Species:</b> no data<br/><b>Watershed:</b> Mad River<br/>Listed in the report with no VFWD data. Blueberry Lake in East Warren is a dam on Mills Brook, so the outlet brook starts at the lake; the lake itself gets stocked brook trout (report p.8, USFS access). Move the pin to the outlet below the dam.<br/><b>Nearest access:</b><ul><li>Blueberry Lake Trails parking (1825 Plunkton Rd, East Warren) &mdash; 0 m as the crow flies, 16.6 min drive</li><li>Austin Brook Trail / Forest Road 25 gate &mdash; 1262 m as the crow flies, 19.8 min drive</li><li>Warren Falls lot (3919 Rte 100) &mdash; 2177 m as the crow flies, 15.9 min drive</li></ul><br/><b>Drive from inn:</b> 16.6 min<br/><b>Source:</b> <a href="https://dec.vermont.gov/sites/dec/files/wsm/mapp/docs/mp_UpperWinooskiWatershedFisheriesSummary_2017-12-15.pdf#page=15">VFWD 2017, narrative p.15</a><br/><b>Confidence:</b> low (Google Places (Blueberry Lake parking) 2026-09-24)]]></description>
