    <Placemark>
      <name>Hedgehog Brook Trailhead (end of Big Basin Rd, North Fayston)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Type:</b> trailhead<br/><b>Parking:</b> Marked lot before the steel gate at the end of the drivable road; trail crosses private land — obey no-parking signs and don't block the gate.<br/>The trail immediately crosses Shepard Brook (ladder + stepping stones; a ford in high water) then climbs beside Hedgehog Brook to the Long Trail / Burnt Rock. Directions: North Fayston Rd west from Rte 100 (4.5 mi north of Rte 17); dirt after 2.5 mi; straight at the 4-way at 4.0 mi onto Big Basin Rd; trailhead at 5.0 mi.<br/><b>Drive from inn:</b> 27.9 min<br/><b>Source:</b> https://www.greenmountainclub.org/hiking/hiking-recommendations/peoples-choice-leaf-peeping-foliage-vermont/ ; https://madrivervalley.com/attraction/burnt-rock-mountain/ ; https://www.pchapin.org/100highest/burnt-rock.html<br/><b>Confidence:</b> high (GP)]]></description>
