    <Placemark>
      <name>Roxbury Fish Culture Station</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Category:</b> landmark<br/>3696 Roxbury Rd (Rte 12A). Vermont's oldest hatchery (1891), rebuilt after Irene and open to visitors; raises brook and rainbow trout. Sits on Flint Brook / Third Branch of the White River, not the Dog — but Rte 12A north from here follows the upper Dog River, brookies-only above Rte 12A per the report.<br/><b>Drive from inn:</b> 24.7 min<br/><b>Source:</b> https://vtfishandwildlife.com/fish/fish-stocking/roxbury-fish-culture-station ; https://roxburyvt.org/roxburyvt-attractions/<br/><b>Confidence:</b> high (Google Places 2026-09-24)]]></description>
